    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the membership-level derivation in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/MembershipLevel.java` to add the tenure factor that grants level 4.\n\n**The change:** The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are now capped at 3, and a fourth level is added only when the owner's tenure exceeds 365 days \u2014 computed as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`.\n\n**Why this satisfies the spec:**\n- A newly created owner's registration date is today (set by `ApplyRegistrationDate`/`RegistrationDate`), so their tenure is 0 days \u2014 they never earn the fourth level and cap at 3.\n- The test's example \u2014 a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` of 0, and a 3-member household \u2014 maxes the pre-tenure factors at 3 and stays there, exactly as `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts (`membershipLevel = 3`).\n- Level 4 becomes reachable only once an owner's registration date is more than a year in the past.\n\nI also updated the class Javadoc (range is now 1\u20134) and left a null-guard on the registration date. Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, tests run 1, failures 0.",
